{"content":[{"c":["NAHSHON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Amminadab’s son; brother of Elisheba and Salmon’s father (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.6.23","r":"Exod.6.23","rawR":"Exod.6.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.6.23","value":"Exod.6.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 6:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.10-11","r":"1Chr.2.10-11","rawR":"1Chr.2.10-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.10-11","value":"1Chr.2.10-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:10-11"},"). Nahshon, the prince of Judah’s tribe at the start of Israel’s wilderness wanderings (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.7","r":"Num.1.7","rawR":"Num.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.7","value":"Num.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 1:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.3","r":"Num.2.3","rawR":"Num.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.3","value":"Num.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.14","r":"Num.10.14","rawR":"Num.10.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.14","value":"Num.10.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:14"},"), represented his kinsmen at the altar’s dedication (",{"href":"?bref=Num.7.12","r":"Num.7.12","rawR":"Num.7.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.7.12","value":"Num.7.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:12"},"). In ",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.20","r":"Ruth.4.20","rawR":"Ruth.4.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.20","value":"Ruth.4.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ruth 4:20"}," he is listed as David’s forefather and a descendant of Judah through the line of Perez, and in Matthew and Luke’s genealogies as an ancestor of Jesus Christ (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.4","r":"Matt.1.4","rawR":"Matt.1.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.4","value":"Matt.1.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.32","r":"Luke.3.32","rawR":"Luke.3.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.32","value":"Luke.3.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:32"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Nahshon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 6:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dict